===Golden Skin Strategies===
*'''For the first quest''', play normally until you see {{CI|Twisted Eclipse|name=true}} on the [[Floor]]. Then, either encounter her normally or ask the distractor to bring Twisted Eclipse to the Elevator. It is easier to do this when she's on the [[Daily Twisted Board]]. Additionally, you should aim for higher Floors, since {{Type|Rare}} [[Twisteds]] become more common.
*'''For the second quest''', play normally but avoid voting for {{CDI|Electrician|name=true}} and try to open all [[Trick or Treat Doors]] on each Floor yourself, or have teammates do so. By doing this you can improve your odds, as there is a chance one of the doors will give the "Did the lights just flicker?" trick, giving you a [[Blackout]].
*'''For the third quest''', get in a team with fast extractors such as {{CI|Shelly|name=true}} or {{CI|Squirm|name=true}} to pass the floors quickly, do this multiple times to get this quest completed fast. You can also choose to play in multiple solo runs, as Eclipse is a very capable solo Toon.

==Strategies==
Due to Eclipse's high [[Movement Speed]] and low [[Stealth]], she works primarily as a distractor. However, her Skill Check and Extraction Speed are average, with 3 {{Star}} on both, letting her do [[Machines]] at moderate speed.

Her Passive [[Ability]], '''Total Eclipse''', increases her max Stamina by 60% and Movement Speed by 20% while in a [[Blackout]], along with giving her a slightly bigger glow. With these buffs combined, Eclipse gains 240 base Stamina and 21/33 base Movement Speed, allowing her to surpass {{CI|Pebble|name=true}} and especially {{CI|Waxwell|name=true}}'s speed and Stamina, and reach the same speed as 1 {{Heart}} {{CI|Looey|name=true}}. Beware however, as she is immobile for 5 seconds when a Blackout starts (due to her transformation animation). During this time she can not be detected and will lose aggro of any [[Twisted]] that had spotted her prior. After this transformation, she highlights all Twisteds on the [[Floor]] for 5 seconds and the player regains control. During Blackouts, her speed can allow her to easily outrun Twisteds like {{CI|Twisted Pebble|name=true}} and {{CI|Twisted Gourdy|name=true}}; using [[Trinkets]] like {{TI|Clown Horn|name=true}} or {{TI|Ribbon Spool|name=true}} can allow her to outwalk Twisted Pebble, though it may not be worth it due to the chance of Blackouts being random (unless you duo distract with another Eclipse).

Even without Trinkets, Eclipse can outwalk all Twisteds during Blackouts (outside of [[Panic Mode]]) aside from {{CI|Twisted Bobette|name=true}}, enraged {{CI|Twisted Glisten|name=true}}, {{CI|Twisted Coal|name=true}} in a Blackout, and Twisted Pebble. However, {{CI|Twisted Vee|name=true}} and her {{Debuff|Slow|II}} could make it a bit harder to distract, especially with limited vision. Also, long-ranged Twisteds like {{CI|Twisted Goob|name=true}} could be problematic so it's suggested to have a backup distractor deal with them.

She's still quite capable at extracting thanks to her average extraction Stats. In such a case, using extraction Trinkets like {{TI|Magnifying Glass|name=true}} or {{TI|Vee's Remote|name=true}} can enhance her capabilities to a more potent extent. Her speed can let her reach Machines more quickly and make it back to the [[Elevator]] during Panic Mode, if she extracts far away from it. She can also utilize her speed to extract Treadmill Machines quite quickly, especially in Blackouts where she could finish them in around 15 seconds, if she only runs. Even while focusing on extracting, she can protect teammates, pass Twisteds to distractors, or help take certain problematic Twisteds like {{CI|Twisted Scraps|name=true}} and distract them, even outside of Blackouts since her non-Blackout speed is still good. Her Ability highlighting Twisteds at the start of a Blackout can also allow her to support her team a bit while being an extractor.

Her larger light radius makes her also capable of surviving and distracting in the dark, though there are other Toons with a larger light radius. Eclipse's higher mobility when combined with having the Light-Producing Aux. Stat makes her one of the best Toons for Blackouts. Though she may not be able to highlight Twisteds throughout the duration of a Floor, she can protect teammates or just generally thrive in Blackouts with little issue.

The best [[Items]] to get depends on how you play as Eclipse. If you're distracting, try to keep at least one Stamina/speed related Item on hand, such as {{II|Pop|name=false|plural=a}} and {{II|Box o' Chocolates|name=true}} in case you have to sprint tap or get afflicted with [[Debuffs]]; keeping a healing Item on hand is also crucial since distracting puts you in harm's way constantly. If you're extracting, getting {{II|Instructions|name=true}} and {{II|Jumper Cable|name=true|plural=a}} can make Eclipse a great extractor, especially if they're paired with extraction Trinkets.

Overall, Eclipse is quite versatile, excelling at distracting, especially in Blackouts. Though, she is also quite capable at extracting. She has great survivability, which combined with the decent extraction makes her a great Toon for solo runs.

